// Phase 3 (INTER), EXPLICIT-COMPOUND DECODE: a REFERENCE_MODE_SELECT frame with
// skip_mode NOT present, where an inter block reads the real compound entropy
// (comp_mode==1). The hierarchical-GOP compound stream at decode index 4 (order
// hint 2) has 4 inter blocks over one 64x64 superblock, all BLOCK_32X32
// (partition SPLIT):
//   * 3 single-ref blocks (NEWMV / NEWMV / NEARESTMV) with TX_32X32 residual.
//   * 1 EXPLICIT-COMPOUND block r=8 c=0 (comp_mode==1): comp_ref_type=BIDIR,
//     ref pair [LAST(1), BWDREF(5)], NEAREST_NEARESTMV, COMPOUND_AVERAGE
//     (comp_group_idx==0). Its 2 MVs come from the compound ref-mv candidate
//     padding built from a REAL single-ref neighbour (refId + sign-biased
//     refDiff): mv0=(-24,-32), mv1=(24,32).
// This decodes that frame to frame-end od_ec sync bit-exact vs the SW reference,
// exercising comp_mode + comp_ref_type + bidir comp_ref pair + compound
// find_mv_refs + interCompoundMode + compound MV resolve + comp_group_idx.

// LAST_FRAME reference index (av1 LAST_FRAME).
